    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Fall risk, reduced (Z91.81)</content>. No falls in six months. Chair stand 12 and tandem stance 10 seconds now meet the norms for her age, and PROMIS physical function is 46, up from 41. Home hazards are corrected. [S]<list><item>Continue the daily exercise program.</item><item>Repeat the STEADI screen yearly, or after any fall.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Lifelong deafblindness (H54.0X55)</content>. Touch, her main channel for language and reading, remains intact. [S]<list><item>Check hand sensation and skin at each wellness visit.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Fall history</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No falls</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Timed Up and Go, 30-second chair stand, and four-stage balance test</td><td>After the exercise program, then yearly</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Timed Up and Go 11.2 seconds, chair stand 12, tandem stance 10 seconds</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>PROMIS physical function</td><td>At assessment and at reviews</td><td>Completed today</td><td>46, up from 41</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>PHQ-9 mood screen</td><td>Yearly and at reviews</td><td>Completed today</td><td>2, completed in braille, with item 9 scored 0</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Home hazard assessment</td><td>After a fall</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Done in July, after the deviation recorded at the three-month review; all changes installed</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Daily strength and balance exercise</td><td>Ongoing</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Daily</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Hand sensation</td><td>Yearly</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Normal</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Medication review for fall-risk drugs</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No regular medicines; nitrofurantoin course completed in August</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Repeat bone density</td><td>In about two years, or if risk changes</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Last done in March</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Qualified tactile interpreter booked by the clinic, double-length visit, braille materials</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Interpreter present for the whole visit; after-visit summary given in braille</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>No further falls, and a 30-second chair stand of 12 or more by the six-month review. Outcome by 1959-09-14: No falls in six months; chair stand 12 [S]</item><item>Home changes complete: handrails on both sides of every step, tactile edge strips, and vibrating smoke and carbon monoxide alarms with a bed shaker. Outcome by 1959-09-14: All installed after the occupational therapy home visit [S]</item><item>A communication access plan in her chart: a qualified tactile interpreter booked by the clinic for every visit, double-length appointments, braille after-visit summaries, and a hospital communication passport. Outcome by 1959-03-23: Plan recorded and passport written in braille and print [S]</item><item>Keep traveling to speak, with a travel plan for falls and illness. Outcome by 1959-09-14: Two speaking trips completed with a sighted guide [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: STEADI (Stopping Elderly Accidents, Deaths and Injuries): Clinical Resources (2024); Falls Prevention in Community-Dwelling Older Adults: Interventions (2024); Zhou SY, et al. Training Medical Students in Deaf, DeafBlind, and Hard-of-Hearing Patient Care Through Interactive Lecture and Simulation. MedEdPORTAL 2025;21:11566 (2025)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Annual wellness visit next month, double length, with an interpreter. Call after any fall. Next scheduled visit 1959-10-19: subsequent annual wellness visit. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
